# yosys 0.55 (VTR build): read_rtlil en.il; opt_dff -keepdc; write_rtlil
# input: Yosys 0.55's own write_rtlil of the `read_verilog -icells` heredoc of tests/opt/opt_dff_en.ys (always-active and never-active EN of every enable FF and latch) in the Yosys source (en.il), with `output [11:0] Q` widened to `[15:0]` (the .ys writes Q[13:12] and Q[15:14] out of range, which Yosys turns into undefined bits), edited by sed in two places: `parameter \\X_POLARITY 1'b` written `b` and `parameter signed \\WIDTH` written `parameter \\WIDTH` (proc_build.c reads plain integer polarity and width parameters; the 2D-1 read_rtlil gap), in every cell. The items below are Yosys's result summarised as test_opt_dff.c's summarize does (cell types with their sorted parameters, constant Q bits; Q bits that alias another net have no item)
# flags: -keepdc
cell $adff ARST_POLARITY=1 ARST_VALUE=2'10 CLK_POLARITY=1 WIDTH=2
cell $and A_SIGNED=0 A_WIDTH=2 B_SIGNED=0 B_WIDTH=2 Y_WIDTH=2
cell $dff CLK_POLARITY=1 WIDTH=2
cell $dffsr CLK_POLARITY=1 CLR_POLARITY=1 SET_POLARITY=0 WIDTH=2
cell $mux WIDTH=2
cell $not A_SIGNED=0 A_WIDTH=2 Y_WIDTH=2
cell $not A_SIGNED=0 A_WIDTH=2 Y_WIDTH=2
cell $or A_SIGNED=0 A_WIDTH=2 B_SIGNED=0 B_WIDTH=2 Y_WIDTH=2
cell $sdff CLK_POLARITY=1 SRST_POLARITY=1 SRST_VALUE=2'10 WIDTH=2
cell $sdff CLK_POLARITY=1 SRST_POLARITY=1 SRST_VALUE=2'10 WIDTH=2
